  "summary_en": "Malaysia's Civil Aviation Regulations 2016 (P.U.(A) 97), bilingual Malay/English, comprehensively regulate aircraft registration, airworthiness, crew licensing, operations, accident investigation and penalties. Part XVI sets permission requirements for unmanned aircraft systems, including drones above 20 kg and small surveillance drones.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Part XVI: unmanned aircraft systems need Director General authorisation in certain airspace classes, within aerodrome traffic zones, or above 400 ft",
   "Small unmanned aircraft (≤20 kg) operators must maintain direct visual contact with the aircraft",
   "Small unmanned surveillance aircraft need permission near designated areas, crowds over 1,000, and within 50 m of persons",
   "UAS above 20 kg require Director General permission",
   "Registration, airworthiness certification, mandatory occurrence reporting and fines/imprisonment enforce compliance"
  ],
